= Priming — Technical =

== Experimental effect ==
A priming effect can be expressed as a change in response metric:

<pre>
priming effect = performance(related/repeated prime)
               − performance(control prime)
</pre>

The sign depends on whether the measure is speed, error, threshold, or another variable.

== Mechanisms ==
Proposed mechanisms include residual activation, predictive processing, facilitated perceptual representation, episodic retrieval, response learning, and expectation.

Different priming paradigms can rely on different mechanisms.

== Semantic priming ==
Semantic priming can vary with stimulus-onset asynchrony, association strength, semantic relation, task, and proportion of related trials.

Automatic and strategic contributions therefore need experimental separation.

== Replication scope ==
Robust lexical/repetition effects should not be used as indirect support for any behaviorally distant "priming" claim.

Phenomenon families need separate evidentiary treatment.

